 twice as many iterations  i did have a like a not a rude awakening  but i was re-appointed with the use of  the horn when i was driving during my  trip to Italy in September because there  with all of the motorcycles and scooters  that are constantly diving in and out  and in between cars their horns are  actually used very regularly sort of as  like a hey I'm here type of of message  like just so you know I'm here because  people are constantly weaving and in the  Amalfi Coast the roads are so narrow and  windy that often you can't  actually see around the curb the curve  rather and the horn is also used to warn  people to sometimes you would drive not  right off to the side but you would  drift sort of to the middle of the road  a little bit because it is so narrow and  when you're coming around these curves  you use your horn just to let oncoming  traffic know that you're there at first  it was very distracting because there's  constant horn honking but it's a totally  different application there yeah and for  the most part that's covered here by  flashing lights right a lot of people if  they're they're warning someone about  something about in the row that's going  on right something that they have to pay  attention to they'll just flash their  lights really quick and I do that all  the time I have one friend who drives  with one hand on the horn because he  wants to be he believes that driving is  sort of like dog training where if you  don't provide the feedback immediately  the the same way the dog doesn't realize  what it's being scolded for unless you  scolded immediately the driver won't  connect whatever action they did to  being scolded by the horn so he drives  with one hand on the wheel at about ten  o'clock and another hand right on the  horn to be able to instantly honk at  other cars I don't know that he's really  doing uh God's work so to speak in  informing people and improving their  driving I think people have no idea what  he's doing but this